# Story animations → Supabase `story-animations`

When producing or updating IQ / toddler / kids story media for this app, keep every finished video and narration in the Supabase Storage bucket named **`story-animations`**.

## Bucket settings

- **Bucket name:** `story-animations`
- **Access:** Public
- **CDN caching:** Enabled (public object URLs)
- Do not put story videos in the `phonics` bucket.

## Object path layout

Match the local public paths so CDN URLs stay stable:

```
story_toddler_01/cover.jpg
story_toddler_01/scene1.mp4
story_toddler_01/scene1.mp3
story_toddler_01/scene2.mp4
…
story_toddler_07/scene2_yellow.mp4
```

Source folder on disk: `public/stories/<story_id>/`

## Compress before upload

Before sending any story or phonics video to a bucket, compress the local MP4s so uploads stay small and reliable.

```bash
node scripts/compress-story-and-phonics-videos.mjs
```

- Compress toddler story videos under `public/stories/**`
- Compress phonics videos under `public/phonics/**`
- Encode one file at a time with H.264, max width 1280, CRF 28, no audio track on silent loops
- Replace the local file only when the compressed version is meaningfully smaller
- Then upload **one compressed file at a time**

## Upload one by one

Upload **one video (or audio) file per request**, wait for success, then send the next. Do not batch-upload many files in parallel.

Reasons:

- Large MP4s fail less often when sent alone
- Progress is clear for the parent review loop
- A failed file can be retried without re-sending the whole story

Preferred command (from the live project root):

```bash
node scripts/upload-story-animations.mjs --one
```

Or upload a single story after it is finished:

```bash
node scripts/upload-story-animations.mjs --story story_toddler_07
```

Credentials required in `.env.local`:

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`

Create the public bucket if it is missing. Upsert on re-upload. Save public URLs to `media/stories/supabase-upload-manifest.json`.

## After upload

- Keep local `public/stories/...` files as the offline fallback.
- Prefer the CDN public URL in story records when the upload succeeded.
- Never commit `.env.local` or service-role keys.
